00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:47.182
Part of the fun of the Scream franchise and the whodunit genre in general

00:07:47.236 --> 00:07:50.174
is going back to see the clues laid out for us once we know the ending.

00:07:50.222 --> 00:07:53.374
In Tara's dialogue with Quinn at the apartment, Quinn describes how her dad

00:07:53.422 --> 00:07:56.530
held on too tight with overprotectiveness after they lost her brother.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:59.974
Combine that with Detective Bailey's line after Quinn's death.

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:03.080
-[Detective Bailey] Both my kids are gone, my whole family is gone.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:09.138
And that's two oddly specific references to this mysterious dead sibling.

00:08:09.234 --> 00:08:12.102
The movie honestly could have used a few red herrings to throw us off

00:08:12.156 --> 00:08:14.502
because it was obvious that this brother was significant.

00:08:14.566 --> 00:08:17.654
Add in the fact that the first Ghostface call comes from Richie Kirsch's

00:08:17.702 --> 00:08:19.498
phone, and it starts to become clear.

00:08:19.584 --> 00:08:23.146
This is the same tactic that Richie and Amber used.

00:08:23.168 --> 00:08:23.802
When a call came in from Amber's phone,

00:08:23.856 --> 00:08:26.606
everyone assumed that the killer cloned Amber's phone number,

00:08:26.628 --> 00:08:29.646
when in reality, all they had to do was use Amber's actual phone.

00:08:29.748 --> 00:08:32.974
Detective Bailey probably got Richie's phone back after his death and just

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:36.766
used that. One area where the movie did successfully employ a red herring was

00:08:36.788 --> 00:08:37.562
in wardrobe.

00:08:37.626 --> 00:08:41.106
Fans know at this point that at least one Ghostface killer always has a

00:08:41.128 --> 00:08:42.542
light blue shirt or flannel.

00:08:42.606 --> 00:08:43.854
In this case, it was Ethan,

00:08:43.902 --> 00:08:47.566
and while I never really suspected Tara or Sam, we're forced to notice Danny

00:08:47.598 --> 00:08:50.070
wearing light blue when we literally see him put it on.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:52.854
Someone wearing a Ghostface mask attacks Sam and Tara outside their apartment,

00:08:52.892 --> 00:08:55.718
the same apartment where they were literally just with Quinn and Ethan.

00:08:55.724 --> 00:08:59.158
Later on, after Quinn's death is staged, her father comes out of the

00:08:59.164 --> 00:09:02.186
building with a little bit of a limp, maybe from an injury sustained when

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:03.782
he's knocked to the floor by Samantha.

00:09:03.846 --> 00:09:08.700
And he's staring right at Samantha as he says this. 

00:09:08.855 --> 00:09:11.062
-[Detective Bailey] You f*** with my family, you die.

00:09:11.126 --> 00:09:13.386
And when Gale gets the dreaded phone call later on.

00:09:13.408 --> 00:09:17.006
It's from a 707 area code, which represents Northern California, where

00:09:17.028 --> 00:09:18.218
Woodsboro is located.

00:09:18.314 --> 00:09:21.550
That's another clue that the killer is from that area, which Richie's family

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:22.702
most likely would be.

00:09:22.756 --> 00:09:25.826
There's also an ominous clue that isn't related to the identity of the protagonist.

00:09:25.848 --> 00:09:29.234
Sam's psychiatrist can be seen watching Invasion of the Body Snatchers

00:09:29.272 --> 00:09:34.046
which literally tells him before he becomes the next Ghostface victim.

00:09:34.078 --> 00:09:37.214
As always, it's one of many horror movie references in a Scream film.

00:09:37.262 --> 00:09:40.514
Every Scream movie makes a reference to Psycho, with the last film

00:09:40.562 --> 00:09:44.146
even containing a Psycho movie poster. That continues here with this poster

00:09:44.178 --> 00:09:45.170
in Jason's apartment.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:48.706
He also has a Vertigo poster, another thriller directed by Alfred Hitchcock.

00:09:48.738 --> 00:09:51.526
In addition to the first Psycho, Psycho Two is also referenced this time. 

00:09:51.558 --> 00:09:54.070
–[Mindy &amp; Kirby] Psycho II is underrated. 

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:57.174
Psycho Two also features a character getting stabbed through the mouth,

00:09:57.222 --> 00:09:59.658
