On top of the mask is the rope that Henry swung from next to a sketch of

00:23:01.084 --> 00:23:03.858
where he was found on the football fields and his obituaries.

00:23:03.954 --> 00:23:07.026
This is an employee shirt from Bradley Video Store, the store that Randy

00:23:07.058 --> 00:23:08.242
worked at in the first movie.

00:23:08.306 --> 00:23:11.926
I'm not positive why this is here, because as far as we know, nobody died at

00:23:11.948 --> 00:23:12.502
the video store.

00:23:12.556 --> 00:23:15.398
But I guess it's possible that it was still a scene in the movie adaptation

00:23:15.414 --> 00:23:15.990
of Stab.

00:23:16.070 --> 00:23:19.110
Rounding out the first movie, we have the Woodsboro High School Flag.

00:23:19.190 --> 00:23:22.138
Scream 2 opens with the Stab movie premiere, and there's a lot of

00:23:22.144 --> 00:23:23.290
memorabilia from that.

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:26.238
We see the costumes, masks and plastic knives that were handed out to

00:23:26.244 --> 00:23:28.574
patrons in attendance at the premiere, as well as a few

00:23:28.612 --> 00:23:29.338
movie tickets.

00:23:29.434 --> 00:23:32.426
In the corner is the giant Ghostface head that decorated the production

00:23:32.458 --> 00:23:33.518
office in Scream 3.

00:23:33.604 --> 00:23:37.566
This sketch depicts Sidney at various points in Scream 2 on stage, in the

00:23:37.588 --> 00:23:39.210
government car, and at the library.

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:41.066
It's above a Windsor College sweater.

00:23:41.098 --> 00:23:44.366
The setting of Scream 2. I believe the camera that Chad picks up and

00:23:44.388 --> 00:23:47.846
throws at Ghostface is Joel's camera during his gig with Up to Date.

00:23:47.948 --> 00:23:51.106
This big old set piece along the side of the theater is the thing that Derek

00:23:51.138 --> 00:23:52.742
was tied to at the end of Scream 2.

00:23:52.796 --> 00:23:56.034
And at some point, we can even see the Agamemnon mask that he was wearing

00:23:56.082 --> 00:23:57.618
when he was lowered onto the stage.

00:23:57.714 --> 00:24:00.102
There's also another mask from that play right here.

00:24:00.156 --> 00:24:03.814
There's also a glimpse of the white blazer that Debbie Salt, Nancy Loomis,

00:24:03.862 --> 00:24:06.762
was wearing during the finale, and I believe this is the gun that she used

00:24:06.816 --> 00:24:07.638
during that scene.

00:24:07.734 --> 00:24:10.666
Scream 3 is all about the production of the third Stab movie being

00:24:10.688 --> 00:24:12.022
terrorized by a new threat.

00:24:12.086 --> 00:24:14.674
Above the Stab 3 script is the slate used during filming.

00:24:14.742 --> 00:24:18.106
However, as an Easter egg, the cinematographer is listed as Brett Jutkiewicz,

00:24:18.138 --> 00:24:21.166
the cinematographer of Scream 2022 and Scream VI.

00:24:21.268 --> 00:24:24.654
I spotted a sketch of Sarah Darling, the first Scream 3 victim, and

00:24:24.692 --> 00:24:26.858
Jennifer Jolie, the actress who played Gale.

00:24:26.954 --> 00:24:29.502
Also visible here is the killer's voice changer and gun.

00:24:29.566 --> 00:24:32.526
Scream 3 had a special voice changer that allowed the user to imitate

00:24:32.558 --> 00:24:33.438
anyone's voice.

00:24:33.534 --> 00:24:36.770
Kind of funny that we've only just recently unlocked that technology today,

00:24:36.840 --> 00:24:40.318
and it's being used to make politicians bicker over video games.

00:24:40.414 --> 00:24:43.714
In this case, there's a melted phone, a frying pan and a lighter.

00:24:43.762 --> 00:24:46.230
The frying pan is the one that the killer used to knock out the security

00:24:46.300 --> 00:24:47.410
guard, Stephen Stone.

00:24:47.490 --> 00:24:50.902
There's another frying pan attack in this movie when Gale uses it against Quinn.

00:24:50.956 --> 00:24:53.110
I wonder if that one will make the next museum.

00:24:53.190 --> 00:24:56.534
The phone is Jennifer Jolie's phone, damaged when her house exploded.

00:24:56.582 --> 00:24:59.414
And the lighter must have been Tom Prince's lighter, which was responsible

00:24:59.462 --> 00:25:00.790
for causing that explosion.

00:25:00.870 --> 00:25:04.186
Overhead is the banner that says, Happy Birthday, Roman, which was displayed

00:25:04.218 --> 00:25:05.946
over the entryway of John Milton's Manor when Sidney arrived.

00:25:05.978 --> 00:25:09.914
It was not a happy birthday for Roman... Scre4m.

00:25:10.042 --> 00:25:13.310
By the time this one rolled around, several more Stab films had been made.

00:25:13.380 --> 00:25:17.246
These posters for Stabs Three, Four and Five are all in Scre4m, but this

00:25:17.268 --> 00:25:20.814
is the first time we've ever seen the Stab Four poster, or should I say the

00:25:20.852 --> 00:25:22.762
St4b poster, unobstructed.

00:25:22.826 --> 00:25:26.198
There are also sketches of the two killers, Charlie and Jill, as well as the

00:25:26.204 --> 00:25:29.414
shirt that Charlie was wearing when he died and the flannel that Jill had on

00:25:29.452 --> 00:25:32.402
before being taken to the hospital and changed into a hospital gown.

00:25:32.466 --> 00:25:35.302
There's a moment where we see Kirby looking at it with tears in her eyes,

00:25:35.356 --> 00:25:38.374
remembering the way that her best friend betrayed her and tried to have her killed.

00:25:38.412 --> 00:25:41.846
And we also see the knife that Charlie stabbed her with and the

00:25:41.868 --> 00:25:44.746
residue on the patio where Kirby was tied up.

00:25:44.768 --> 00:25:48.342
In the back, here you'll see the outfit worn by Jill's ex-boyfriend, Trevor, when he died.

00:25:48.406 --> 00:25:52.074
It could also potentially be Neil Prescott's outfit from Scream One, which

00:25:52.112 --> 00:25:52.762
looks the same.

00:25:52.816 --> 00:25:55.954
But since Neil never died, I'm guessing he got to keep his clothes.

00:25:56.022 --> 00:25:58.666
I see no reason they would have ended up in police custody.

00:25:58.778 --> 00:26:00.446
This one was the hardest to place.

00:26:00.548 --> 00:26:03.674
My first thought was that it was supposed to be Casey Becker, because nobody

00:26:03.722 --> 00:26:05.434
else died in a white long sleeve.

00:26:05.482 --> 00:26:08.110
But it doesn't match, and she wasn't wearing shorts.

00:26:08.190 --> 00:26:11.214
My guess is that it's actually supposed to be Jill's neighbor, Olivia Morris,

00:26:11.262 --> 00:26:14.286
who was taken down while wearing a gray long sleeve and flannel shorts.

00:26:14.318 --> 00:26:17.106
It's not a perfect match, but it's my best guess.

00:26:17.208 --> 00:26:20.406
There's also a Woodsboro police uniform, meaning that this belonged to

00:26:20.428 --> 00:26:24.066
Deputy Hoss or Deputy Perkins, the two cops who fell in the line of duty

00:26:24.098 --> 00:26:25.798
while parked outside of Jill's house.

00:26:25.884 --> 00:26:27.842
And we have a Stabathon t-shirt.

00:26:27.906 --> 00:26:30.978
Stabathon was the movie marathon event hosted by the Woodsboro High Film Club,

00:26:30.994 --> 00:26:33.270
where Gale Weathers was nearly butchered.

00:26:33.350 --> 00:26:36.698
In addition to those, there's also a case full of Gale's books, most of

00:26:36.704 --> 00:26:40.970
which we've seen before in Scream 3 and Four, with one notable addition.

00:26:50.430 --> 00:26:53.822
The Gale Weathers book that we haven't seen before is Stabbed in the Back:

00:26:53.876 --> 00:26:54.814
The Real Sunrise Story.

00:26:54.932 --> 00:26:58.050
This actually comes from one of the promotional websites for Scream 3,

00:26:58.120 --> 00:26:59.150
Sunrise Sucks.

00:26:59.230 --> 00:27:02.446
This was an anonymous expose site that published dirt about the production

00:27:02.478 --> 00:27:05.454
company responsible for the Stab franchise, Sunrise Studios.

00:27:05.502 --> 00:27:08.546
I talk about it extensively in my Horror History episode on the history of

00:27:08.568 --> 00:27:09.518
the Stab IP.

00:27:09.614 --> 00:27:12.566
By the way, in Gale's apartment, there's one new book called

00:27:12.588 --> 00:27:15.398
The Woodsboro Horror Continues, which must be the one she wrote about the

00:27:15.404 --> 00:27:18.642
2022 or whenever it took place, Woodsboro Massacre.

00:27:18.706 --> 00:27:21.906
All of these theater shrine items were part of Richie Kirsch's collection,

00:27:22.018 --> 00:27:24.906
despite the fact that he claims that the first Stab movie is the only good one.

00:27:24.928 --> 00:27:28.554
He dies in Scream 2022, so it makes sense that there wouldn't be much

00:27:28.592 --> 00:27:29.302
from that movie.

00:27:29.366 --> 00:27:32.666
However, I did notice the Stab Blu-ray box-set, which was released at some

00:27:32.688 --> 00:27:34.458
point between Screams Four and Five.

00:27:34.544 --> 00:27:37.294
If there's one thing you can usually count on in a requel, it's the new

00:27:37.332 --> 00:27:39.786
characters taking up the mantle of the legacy characters.

00:27:39.898 --> 00:27:43.246
In the case of Scream, Sam Carpenter is the new Sidney Prescott, and she

00:27:43.268 --> 00:27:46.250
puts on the Ghostface costume to fight back against Detective Bailey at the

00:27:46.260 --> 00:27:46.942
end of the movie.

00:27:47.006 --> 00:27:50.482
It's the very same Ghostface costume that Sidney wore to strike back against

00:27:50.536 --> 00:27:53.102
Billy Loomis approximately 27 years earlier.

00:27:53.166 --> 00:27:56.858
And just like Billy, Bailey finds himself on the wrong end of a Ghostface

00:27:56.894 --> 00:27:58.230
call from his prey.

00:28:00.490 --> 00:28:02.550
-[Sam] Hello, Detective Bailey.

00:28:04.170 --> 00:28:08.854
-[Sam] Are you alone in the house? 

00:28:08.892 --> 00:28:12.666
Bailey is not the only one to suffer a very 1996 fate, Ethan pops up in the final reel

00:28:12.688 --> 00:28:14.950
for one last scare and gets crushed by the same TV that fell upon Stu Macher.

00:28:15.030 --> 00:28:18.410
So what's the message this time? What are the filmmakers trying to tell us?

00:28:18.480 --> 00:28:20.710
Well, it's not that different from the last movie.

00:28:20.790 --> 00:28:23.734
This is kind of the second one in a row that condemns toxic Internet

00:28:23.782 --> 00:28:27.086
culture. This time, instead of toxic fandom, it's about the phenomenon of

00:28:27.108 --> 00:28:30.238
Reddit detectives who try to solve crimes on their own and usually just end

00:28:30.244 --> 00:28:31.322
up making things worse.

00:28:31.386 --> 00:28:34.478
Wavywebsurf has a really good video on the topic if you want to learn more.

00:28:34.564 --> 00:28:37.694
Throughout the movie, Sam has to deal with accusations that she was actually

00:28:37.732 --> 00:28:41.006
the killer in Woodsboro, like this guy who refers to her as being that

00:28:41.028 --> 00:28:41.790
psycho girl.

00:28:41.860 --> 00:28:43.722
He looks like he could be an actual Redditor.

00:28:43.786 --> 00:28:47.478
Another chick recognizes her, dumps diet Cherry Coke on her, and calls her a murderer.

00:28:47.484 --> 00:28:50.278
Why would you dump a beverage on someone if you believe she was a

00:28:50.284 --> 00:28:52.038
murderer? That is not a smart move.

00:28:52.124 --> 00:28:54.662
Even her psychiatrist starts to get creeped out by her.

00:28:54.716 --> 00:28:57.446
If you're like me, you probably wanted to go back and look at the names in

00:28:57.468 --> 00:29:00.354
the psychiatrist's filing cabinet to see if there were any Easter eggs.

00:29:00.402 --> 00:29:03.526
As far as I can tell, these are just random patient names with no deeper meaning.

00:29:03.558 --> 00:29:06.618
But Mars Jupiter is definitely a weird one.

00:29:06.704 --> 00:29:09.286
Perhaps the biggest twist with this movie is that none of the core

00:29:09.318 --> 00:29:10.134
characters died.

00:29:10.182 --> 00:29:13.126
It looked like Chad was a goner there for a minute, but he miraculously

00:29:13.158 --> 00:29:14.730
makes it out on a stretcher at the end.

00:29:14.800 --> 00:29:17.886
Although during that part where Tara takes off his oxygen mask to kiss him,

00:29:17.908 --> 00:29:19.614
I wish he just would have died right there.

00:29:19.732 --> 00:29:22.170
It would have been so ******* funny.

